1
00:00:09,970 --> 00:00:14,970
Hi there, this is lecture 4 in the Introduction to Photonics video series.
大家好，这是光子学入门系列视频的第 4 讲。

2
00:00:14,970 --> 00:00:19,970
The title of this lecture is More on Properties of Light.
本讲的题目是“光的性质续论”。

3
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:24,970
In the previous three lectures, we laid foundations of photonics.
在前三讲中，我们奠定了光子学的基础。

4
00:00:24,970 --> 00:00:28,970
We established the terminology that describes the light.
我们建立了描述光的术语。

5
00:00:28,970 --> 00:00:31,970
We talked about different properties of light.
我们讲了光的各种性质。

6
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:34,970
We established the dual nature of light.
我们确立了光的二象性。

7
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:38,970
We talked about absorption and emission in the previous lecture.
在上一讲中，我们讲了吸收和发射。

8
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:43,970
This lecture number 4 takes us one step further.
第 4 讲带我们再前进一步。

9
00:00:43,970 --> 00:00:49,970
We are going to expand on the topics related to the properties of light.
我们将展开讲与光的性质有关的话题。

10
00:00:49,970 --> 00:00:55,970
We are going to expand on the stuff that we talked about in the previous three lectures.
我们将展开讲前三讲中讲过的内容。

11
00:00:55,970 --> 00:01:02,970
Specifically, in this lecture, we are going to cover topics that are going to help us better understand
具体来说，在本讲中，我们将讲一些话题，帮助我们更好地理解

12
00:01:02,970 --> 00:01:08,970
the nature of optical materials and their transmission and reflection characteristics as a function of the wavelength.
光学材料的本质，以及它们的透射和反射特性随波长的变化。

13
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:17,970
We are also going to talk about the selection of optical materials for specific use in the visible ultraviolet or infrared region.
我们还将讲如何选择光学材料，用于可见光、紫外或红外区域的特定用途。

14
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:24,970
Finally, we are going to explain how a single and multiple anti-reflection coatings and filters are made and used.
最后，我们将解释单层和多层增透膜以及滤光片是如何制作和使用的。

15
00:01:24,970 --> 00:01:30,970
With this lecture, we are slowly moving in the direction of an optical lab.
通过本讲，我们正慢慢地向光学实验室的方向迈进。

16
00:01:30,970 --> 00:01:40,970
We are going to start talking about optical components and different amounts that are to be found in a standard optical lab.
我们将开始讲标准光学实验室中可以见到的光学元件和各种镜架。

17
00:01:40,970 --> 00:01:52,970
We are going to try to make a transition from the basic theoretical foundations of photonics into more of a practical concept.
我们将尝试从光子学的基础理论过渡到更偏实用的概念。

18
00:01:53,970 --> 00:02:01,970
The first concept that we are going to mention is the optical materials that are to be found in an optical lab.
我们要提到的第一个概念是光学实验室中可以见到的光学材料。

19
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:07,970
We are going to find a large variety of different optical materials and different optical components.
我们会见到种类繁多的不同光学材料和不同光学元件。

20
00:02:07,970 --> 00:02:15,970
In general, we can classify them in so-called non-transparent and also so-called transparent types of optical materials.
一般来说，我们可以把它们分为所谓的不透明光学材料和所谓的透明光学材料。

21
00:02:15,970 --> 00:02:20,970
We are going to define each of these throughout this lecture.
我们将在本讲中分别给出它们的定义。

22
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:24,970
The first that we are going to talk about is the transparent optical medium.
我们首先要讲的是透明光学介质。

23
00:02:24,970 --> 00:02:27,970
Everyone knows what transparent means.
大家都知道透明是什么意思。

24
00:02:27,970 --> 00:02:32,970
The most popular definition when we say transparent means something that we can see through.
我们说“透明”时，最常见的定义是指我们能透过它看东西。

25
00:02:32,970 --> 00:02:39,970
But if you want to kind of be more specific and use the term from the field of photonics,
但如果你想说得更具体一些，用光子学领域的术语来说，

26
00:02:39,970 --> 00:02:48,970
we are going to define transparent optical medium as a medium that has a low absorption, low reflection,
我们把透明光学介质定义为这样一种介质：它的吸收低、反射低，

27
00:02:49,970 --> 00:02:55,970
distortion of light that's passing through it is reduced to a minimum.
通过它的光的畸变被降到最低。

28
00:02:55,970 --> 00:03:00,970
It also would have a high damage threshold for laser radiation.
它对激光辐射还具有很高的损伤阈值。

29
00:03:00,970 --> 00:03:05,970
And finally, it's going to have a minimal optical degradation to different environmental effects,
最后，它在各种环境影响下的光学性能退化极小，

30
00:03:05,970 --> 00:03:11,970
such as temperature, water vapor, and other hostile environment conditions.
比如温度、水蒸气以及其他恶劣的环境条件。

31
00:03:11,970 --> 00:03:17,970
On this slide, we are going to further expand on the topic of our index of refraction.
在这张幻灯片上，我们将进一步展开讲折射率这个话题。

32
00:03:18,970 --> 00:03:21,970
In one of the previous lectures, we defined index of refraction.
在前面的一讲中，我们定义了折射率。

33
00:03:21,970 --> 00:03:28,970
We said that index of refraction represents a unitless quantity that characterizes a specific medium.
我们说过，折射率是一个表征某种特定介质的无量纲量。

34
00:03:28,970 --> 00:03:35,970
Every medium has a specific index of refraction that defines optical properties of that material.
每种介质都有特定的折射率，它决定了该材料的光学性质。

35
00:03:35,970 --> 00:03:42,970
To be more specific, index of refraction represents the number that shows us how much is the speed of light
更具体地说，折射率是一个数，它告诉我们光速

36
00:03:42,970 --> 00:03:48,970
reduced in that specific medium relative to the speed of light in air or vacuum.
在该特定介质中相对于空气或真空中的光速降低了多少。

37
00:03:48,970 --> 00:03:54,970
So once more, index of refraction or refractive index is defined as the ratio of the speed of light
所以再说一遍，折射率被定义为光在

38
00:03:54,970 --> 00:03:58,970
in a vacuum to the speed of light in a particular medium.
真空中的速度与光在某一特定介质中的速度之比。

39
00:03:58,970 --> 00:04:04,970
We are talking about a unitless quantity that's always greater than 1.
我们说的是一个总是大于 1 的无量纲量。

40
00:04:04,970 --> 00:04:10,970
If index of refraction is equal to 1, it means that we are talking about the vacuum,
如果折射率等于 1，就意味着我们说的是真空，

41
00:04:10,970 --> 00:04:17,970
we are talking about the medium that has a speed of light equal to the 3 times 10 to the 8 meters per second.
我们说的是光速等于每秒 3 乘 10 的 8 次方米的介质。

42
00:04:17,970 --> 00:04:26,970
It's also important to understand that the index of refraction is also going to be a function of the wavelength.
还要理解的重要一点是，折射率也是波长的函数。

43
00:04:26,970 --> 00:04:32,970
That's something new that we haven't mentioned before, and we are introducing on this specific slide.
这是我们以前没有提到过的新内容，我们在这张幻灯片上介绍它。

44
00:04:32,970 --> 00:04:46,970
So if you're looking at a plot on our right-hand side, we see here two plots, three plots, three curves for three different types of material.
所以如果你看右边的图，我们这里看到两条、三条曲线，对应三种不同的材料。

45
00:04:46,970 --> 00:04:52,970
On the top we have a crown glass, and then we have acrylic, and finally on the bottom we have a fused quartz.
最上面是冕牌玻璃，然后是亚克力，最下面是熔融石英。

46
00:04:52,970 --> 00:05:02,970
On a horizontal x-axis are different wavelengths that are covering a visible spectrum ranging from 400 nanometers all the way to 700 nanometers,
水平的 x 轴上是覆盖可见光谱的不同波长，从 400 纳米一直到 700 纳米，

47
00:05:02,970 --> 00:05:07,970
and then on the vertical axis we have the index of refraction.
然后在纵轴上是折射率。

48
00:05:07,970 --> 00:05:14,970
You can see that these three curves are not flat. In other words, the index of refraction is changing with the wavelength.
你可以看到这三条曲线并不平坦。换句话说，折射率随波长而变化。

49
00:05:14,970 --> 00:05:21,970
So for example, if you're looking at acrylic, which is a very popular type of medium used in many optical components in a photonics lab,
所以例如，如果你看亚克力，它是一种非常常用的介质，用于光子学实验室的许多光学元件，

50
00:05:21,970 --> 00:05:35,970
we see that at the wavelength of red, the wavelength of violet, which is 400 nanometers, the index of refraction of acrylic is about 1.51.
我们看到在红光的波长，在紫光的波长，也就是 400 纳米处，亚克力的折射率约为 1.51。

51
00:05:35,970 --> 00:05:43,970
And if you are going all the way to the right side, if you come closer to the 700 nanometers, which is the wavelength of red,
如果你一直往右边走，接近 700 纳米，也就是红光的波长，

52
00:05:43,970 --> 00:05:52,970
we see that index of refraction of acrylic dropped from 1.51 all the way down to below 1.49.
我们看到亚克力的折射率从 1.51 一直降到 1.49 以下。

53
00:05:52,970 --> 00:06:05,970
So these differences are relatively small, so we're talking here about the range of change from 1.51 to 1.49 in the case of acrylic,
所以这些差异相对较小，对于亚克力，我们这里说的是从 1.51 到 1.49 的变化范围，

54
00:06:05,970 --> 00:06:12,970
but they are enough to produce a certain effect that we can very easily observe.
但它们足以产生一种我们很容易观察到的效应。

55
00:06:12,970 --> 00:06:21,970
For example, if we have a prism that's made out of acrylic, if you're shooting the different colors of light,
例如，如果我们有一个用亚克力做的棱镜，如果你射入不同颜色的光，

56
00:06:21,970 --> 00:06:30,970
those different colors will be refracted at different angles due to the fact that index of refraction is different for those different colors.
这些不同的颜色会以不同的角度折射，因为不同颜色对应的折射率不同。

57
00:06:30,970 --> 00:06:43,970
In other words, if we are shooting white light through the prism made out of acrylic, what you'll see on the other side is that that white is going to be broken down into all the colors that it's made out of.
换句话说，如果我们让白光通过用亚克力做的棱镜，你会在另一侧看到白光被分解成组成它的所有颜色。

58
00:06:43,970 --> 00:06:49,970
And that's exactly practical application of the concept that we're introducing on this specific slide.
而这正是我们在这张幻灯片上介绍的概念的实际应用。

59
00:06:49,970 --> 00:07:00,970
So once more, index of refraction is a unit list quantity that describes the ratio of the speed of light in the vacuum to the speed of light in a specific medium.
所以再说一遍，折射率是一个无量纲量，它描述的是光在真空中的速度与光在某一特定介质中的速度之比。

60
00:07:00,970 --> 00:07:18,970
And this unit list quantity is a function of the wavelength. In other words, it's changing with the wavelength. What we see on the right hand side is an example with three curves representing three different types of optical materials that are very popular materials used in photonics.
而这个无量纲量是波长的函数。换句话说，它随波长而变化。我们在右边看到的是一个例子，有三条曲线，代表光子学中非常常用的三种不同光学材料。

61
00:07:19,970 --> 00:07:25,970
The next topic that we are going to expand in this lecture is a concept of absorption and transmission of light.
本讲要展开的下一个话题是光的吸收和透射的概念。

62
00:07:25,970 --> 00:07:31,970
In the previous lecture, number three, we talked about particle properties of light.
在上一讲，即第三讲中，我们讲了光的粒子性。

63
00:07:31,970 --> 00:07:40,970
And we translated those properties into specific phenomena that relate to the light, specifically interaction of light and the medium.
我们把这些性质转化为与光有关的具体现象，特别是光与介质的相互作用。

64
00:07:40,970 --> 00:07:57,970
And we said that if light passes through a medium, an absorption phenomenon is taking place where the power of the light beam is being reduced as the light is propagating through that medium.
我们说过，如果光通过某种介质，就会发生吸收现象，光束在该介质中传播时，其功率会降低。

65
00:07:57,970 --> 00:08:07,970
And why is that happening has been explained in the previous lecture. We talked about atomic model of a material.
为什么会这样，在上一讲中已经解释过了。我们讲了材料的原子模型。

66
00:08:07,970 --> 00:08:17,970
We talked about different energy levels of different electrons, how they're moving from our lower to higher energy levels as they're absorbing the light, etc.
我们讲了不同电子的不同能级，讲了它们在吸收光时如何从较低能级移到较高能级，等等。

67
00:08:17,970 --> 00:08:21,970
So on this slide, we are going to quantify that whole concept.
所以在这张幻灯片上，我们要把整个概念定量化。

68
00:08:22,970 --> 00:08:33,970
So what you see on the right hand side is a plot of an optical window of a thickness x. So this optical window is made out of certain material.
你在右边看到的是一块厚度为 x 的光学窗口的示意图。这块光学窗口由某种材料制成。

69
00:08:33,970 --> 00:08:42,970
And the property of material is specified through this so-called absorbing material coefficient alpha.
而材料的性质通过这个所谓的材料吸收系数 α 来表示。

70
00:08:42,970 --> 00:08:47,970
So this number alpha is changing with different media.
所以这个数 α 随介质不同而变化。

71
00:08:47,970 --> 00:08:53,970
From the left hand side, we have an incident light that carries a certain power.
从左边来的是携带一定功率的入射光。

72
00:08:53,970 --> 00:09:00,970
And here we are also going to introduce the concept of so-called irradiance. Irradiance represents the power over the area.
这里我们还要引入所谓辐照度的概念。辐照度表示单位面积上的功率。

73
00:09:00,970 --> 00:09:10,970
So if you are, for example, looking at two different laser beams, and let's say both of those laser beams are carrying power of 10 watts.
所以例如，如果你看两束不同的激光束，假设这两束激光的功率都是 10 瓦。

74
00:09:10,970 --> 00:09:21,970
However, one of the laser beams is very wide, while the other one is very thin.
但是，其中一束激光很宽，而另一束很细。

75
00:09:21,970 --> 00:09:35,970
The effect that a thin laser beam is going to make on the material is going to be much larger than the effect that a wider beam is going to make, although both of them are carrying the same power of 10 watts.
细激光束对材料产生的效应会比宽光束产生的效应大得多，尽管两者携带的功率都是 10 瓦。

76
00:09:35,970 --> 00:09:56,970
So in order to capture that type of effect, we have to look at a different quantity that's going to take into account both the power on the one side and then also the area or the thickness or if you wish, the width of the beam of that light.
所以为了描述这类效应，我们必须看另一个量，它一方面考虑功率，另一方面还考虑光束的面积，或者说粗细，或者如果你愿意，也可以说是光束的宽度。

77
00:09:56,970 --> 00:10:04,970
And that quantity is so-called irradiance. So we define irradiance as a power of a specific area.
这个量就是所谓的辐照度。所以我们把辐照度定义为单位面积上的功率。

78
00:10:04,970 --> 00:10:20,970
So this incident light that you're seeing here coming from the left side and entering the optical window is going to have a specific irradiance, E0, and it also is specified by the wavelength lambda.
所以你在这里看到的这束从左边来、进入光学窗口的入射光，会有一个特定的辐照度 E0，它还由波长 λ 来表征。

79
00:10:20,970 --> 00:10:32,970
What we also see is that same beam of light exits the optical window. We see that irradiance changed. It's not anymore E0.
我们还看到，同一束光从光学窗口射出。我们看到辐照度改变了，不再是 E0。

80
00:10:32,970 --> 00:10:42,970
Now it is equal to capital E. In other words, the irradiance has changed because a certain amount of power has been absorbed in this optical medium.
现在它等于大写 E。换句话说，辐照度改变了，因为有一定的功率在这种光学介质中被吸收了。

81
00:10:42,970 --> 00:10:54,970
The question is how we can quantify, how we can calculate what is the power, what is the irradiance on the right side compared to the irradiance on the left side.
问题是我们如何定量描述、如何计算右边的功率、右边的辐照度与左边的辐照度相比是多少。

82
00:10:54,970 --> 00:11:04,970
What is the comparison between the output power that exits the optical window and the input power that enters this optical window?
从光学窗口射出的输出功率与进入这块光学窗口的输入功率相比如何？

83
00:11:04,970 --> 00:11:18,970
It turns out that there is a specific formula, there is a specific law that's shown here in a box on the left-hand side where the output irradiance E is a function of the input irradiance E0
结果表明，有一个专门的公式，有一条专门的定律，显示在左边的方框中，其中输出辐照度 E 是输入辐照度 E0 的函数，

84
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:29,970
and then also a function of the type of material that's captured to the coefficient alpha and then also is a function of the thickness of the window that's captured to the parameter x.
也是材料类型的函数，材料类型由系数 α 体现，同时还是窗口厚度的函数，窗口厚度由参数 x 体现。

85
00:11:29,970 --> 00:11:37,970
So once more E0, capital E0 represents the incident irradiance, incident power per unit area.
所以再说一遍，E0，大写 E0，表示入射辐照度，即单位面积上的入射功率。

86
00:11:37,970 --> 00:11:44,970
Capital E is going to capture the transmitted irradiance or the output irradiance.
大写 E 表示透射辐照度，或者说输出辐照度。

87
00:11:44,970 --> 00:11:58,970
Alpha is an absorption coefficient in the units of reciprocal length that captures the properties of the material that optical window is made out of and finally x represents the thickness of the optical window.
α 是吸收系数，单位是长度的倒数，它体现了光学窗口所用材料的性质，最后 x 表示光学窗口的厚度。

88
00:11:58,970 --> 00:12:09,970
And we see that through the formula, through the law that's being shown here, the output irradiance is going to be the function of the input irradiance,
我们看到，通过这个公式，通过这里所示的这条定律，输出辐照度是输入辐照度、

89
00:12:09,970 --> 00:12:16,970
type of material that optical window is made out of and finally thickness of that window.
光学窗口所用材料的类型以及窗口厚度的函数。

90
00:12:16,970 --> 00:12:33,970
We can also define so-called transmittance. The transmittance is basically a representation of how much percentage wise of the input power has been transmitted over to the other side of this optical window.
我们还可以定义所谓的透射率。透射率基本上表示输入功率中有百分之多少透射到了这块光学窗口的另一侧。

91
00:12:33,970 --> 00:12:44,970
So if we take a ratio of the output irradiance E and the input irradiance E0 and multiply by 100, we are going to get so-called transmittance.
所以如果我们取输出辐照度 E 与输入辐照度 E0 之比，再乘以 100，就得到所谓的透射率。

92
00:12:44,970 --> 00:12:48,970
That's going to be the percentage quantity.
它是一个百分比量。

93
00:12:48,970 --> 00:13:09,970
So it's very easy if we apply the formula from the previous slide to see that this transmittance, the quantity transmittance, is going to be determined by the properties of this optical window and also the thickness of the window.
所以如果我们应用上一张幻灯片中的公式，很容易看出，这个透射率，透射率这个量，是由这块光学窗口的性质以及窗口的厚度决定的。

94
00:13:09,970 --> 00:13:18,970
So we can also observe that the absorption coefficient alpha depends on the nature of the material and the wavelength of the light.
所以我们还可以观察到，吸收系数 α 取决于材料的性质和光的波长。

95
00:13:18,970 --> 00:13:30,970
It's also important to mention that most of the optical glass materials, transparent materials that are being used in photonics labs, would transmit nearly 100% of the visible light,
还要提到的重要一点是，光子学实验室中使用的大多数光学玻璃材料、透明材料，几乎能透过 100% 的可见光，

96
00:13:30,970 --> 00:13:36,970
meaning the entire range from the near ultraviolet all the way to the near infrared.
也就是从近紫外一直到近红外的整个范围。

97
00:13:36,970 --> 00:13:47,970
