所以如果你在光子学实验室中进行涉及这些材料的某些类型的实验，这类表格就会变得非常有用。

119
00:18:20,970 --> 00:18:30,970
Starting with this slide, we are shifting our focus from absorption and transmission to the concept of surface reflection.
从这张幻灯片开始，我们把注意力从吸收和透射转到表面反射的概念上。

120
00:18:30,970 --> 00:18:41,970
So we are still looking at the boundary between the two media, as shown in the picture on the left side.
所以我们仍然看两种介质之间的边界，如左边的图所示。

121
00:18:41,970 --> 00:18:50,970
You can see that here we are dealing with the air on the left-hand side, and we are dealing with the glass on the right-hand side.
你可以看到，这里左边是空气，右边是玻璃。

122
00:18:50,970 --> 00:18:57,970
Each of these two media are characterized by the index of refraction. In the case of air, we are dealing with the index of refraction equal to one.
这两种介质各自用折射率来表征。对于空气，折射率等于 1。

123
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:05,970
And then, in the case of a glass, we are dealing with a type of glass that has index of refraction equal to 1.5.
然后对于玻璃，我们这里是一种折射率等于 1.5 的玻璃。

124
00:19:05,970 --> 00:19:14,970
So what are we interested in this case here is what is happening when the light hits the boundary between the air and the glass.
所以在这种情况下，我们感兴趣的是光照射到空气和玻璃之间的边界时会发生什么。

125
00:19:14,970 --> 00:19:22,970
We know that, according to the wave properties, there is going to be a certain reflection of light from this boundary.
我们知道，根据波动性质，光会在这个边界上发生一定的反射。

126
00:19:22,970 --> 00:19:28,970
We can use the law of reflection to determine the direction of the reflected beam.
我们可以用反射定律来确定反射光束的方向。

127
00:19:28,970 --> 00:19:40,970
But what we are interested on this slide to determine is what is the power, what is the irradiance that is in that reflected beam.
但我们在这张幻灯片上想确定的是，反射光束中的功率是多少，辐照度是多少。

128
00:19:40,970 --> 00:19:50,970
So that's what is basically being represented on this picture that's shown on the left-hand side.
所以这基本上就是左边这张图所表示的内容。

129
00:19:50,970 --> 00:20:02,970
It turns out that reflection, or so-called reflectance, which is going to basically be equal to the percentage of the input power that's being reflected,
结果表明，反射，或者说所谓的反射率，它基本上等于输入功率中被反射的百分比，

130
00:20:02,970 --> 00:20:06,970
is a function of the two indices of refraction of the two media.
是两种介质的两个折射率的函数。

131
00:20:06,970 --> 00:20:12,970
So the formula, the equation that you are seeing on the right-hand side, defines so-called reflectance.
所以你在右边看到的公式、方程，定义了所谓的反射率。

132
00:20:12,970 --> 00:20:21,970
So once more, reflectance is equal to the ratio of the reflected irradiance to the input irradiance or incident irradiance.
所以再说一遍，反射率等于反射辐照度与输入辐照度或入射辐照度之比。

133
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:28,970
And it's a function of the two numbers, N1 and N2, according to the equation that you are seeing on the right-hand side.
根据你在右边看到的方程，它是 N1 和 N2 这两个数的函数。

134
00:20:29,970 --> 00:20:40,970
So if we plug in the values for the index of refraction, N1 equal to 1, and index of refraction equal to 1.5 for the second medium,
所以如果我们代入折射率的值，N1 等于 1，第二种介质的折射率等于 1.5，

135
00:20:40,970 --> 00:20:46,970
and do calculation, we are going to come up with the value of reflectance being equal to 4%.
然后进行计算，就会得到反射率等于 4%。

136
00:20:47,970 --> 00:20:56,970
This number 4% means that out of the total input irradiance that is in an incident ray, 4% is going to get reflected,
4% 这个数意味着，在入射光线的全部输入辐照度中，有 4% 会被反射，

137
00:20:56,970 --> 00:21:02,970
while the rest of 96% is going to get transmitted into the glass.
而其余 96% 会透射进入玻璃。

138
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:15,970
And then as this transmitted ray that's equal to 96% of the incident irradiance is going to be absorbed slowly as the light beam is moving through the glass.
然后，这条等于入射辐照度 96% 的透射光线，在光束穿过玻璃的过程中会被慢慢吸收。

139
00:21:15,970 --> 00:21:27,970
So using the formula on the right-hand side, we have determined the reflectance at the boundary between the air and the glass
所以利用右边的公式，我们确定了空气和玻璃之间边界上的反射率，

140
00:21:27,970 --> 00:21:36,970
as a function of the two indices of refraction of the first medium, in our case air, and the second medium in our case glass.
它是第一种介质（在我们这里是空气）和第二种介质（在我们这里是玻璃）这两个折射率的函数。

141
00:21:36,970 --> 00:21:40,970
The next case that we are going to analyze is a case of an optical window.
我们要分析的下一种情况是光学窗口的情况。

142
00:21:40,970 --> 00:21:53,970
So in this case, we not only have the first boundary between the air and the glass, but also the second boundary from the glass back into the air.
所以在这种情况下，我们不仅有从空气到玻璃的第一个边界，还有从玻璃回到空气的第二个边界。

143
00:21:53,970 --> 00:22:03,970
So what of interest here is, again, how much light is going to get reflected from such an optical window.
所以这里我们感兴趣的仍然是，从这样一块光学窗口会反射多少光。

144
00:22:04,970 --> 00:22:18,970
What's important to notice here is that we don't have just one single reflection, as in the case of the single boundary between the air and the glass,
这里需要注意的重要一点是，我们不是只有一次反射，不像空气和玻璃之间只有一个边界的情况，

145
00:22:18,970 --> 00:22:24,970
but we have all these multiple reflections. How are these multiple reflections established?
而是有所有这些多次反射。这些多次反射是怎么形成的呢？

146
00:22:24,970 --> 00:22:26,970
So let's look at the incident light beam.
我们来看入射光束。

147
00:22:26,970 --> 00:22:42,970
So this incident light beam is going to hit the first boundary, and there's going to be a first single reflection that we calculated in the previous case to be equal to 4% in the case of a glass being equal to 1.5.
这束入射光束会照射到第一个边界上，会有第一次反射，我们在前面的情况中算出，当玻璃为 1.5 时，它等于 4%。

148
00:22:42,970 --> 00:22:51,970
Now, the rest of the irradiance is going to get transmitted into the window, is going to continue propagating towards the right side.
现在，其余的辐照度会透射进入窗口，继续向右传播。

149
00:22:51,970 --> 00:23:07,970
And then when that light beam reaches the second boundary between the glass and the air, a certain amount of that power is going to get reflected back into the window while the rest is going to be transmitted into the air.
然后当这束光到达玻璃和空气之间的第二个边界时，一部分功率会被反射回窗口内，而其余部分会透射进入空气。

150
00:23:07,970 --> 00:23:16,970
So the reflected amount of light that's from the second boundary is going to propagate back towards the first boundary.
所以从第二个边界反射的那部分光会向回传播到第一个边界。

151
00:23:16,970 --> 00:23:30,970
And then the first boundary, a certain amount is going to get reflected back into the window, but also a certain amount is going to get transmitted into the air, and it's going to show up as the second reflection.
然后在第一个边界上，一部分会被反射回窗口内，但也有一部分会透射进入空气，作为第二次反射出现。

152
00:23:30,970 --> 00:23:41,970
And then we have all this bouncing back and forth of the light. So the light is going to be bouncing back and forth in the window, a certain amount of that light is going to get transmitted, a certain amount of that light is going to get reflected.
然后光就这样来回反弹。所以光会在窗口中来回反弹，其中一部分光会透射出去，一部分光会被反射。

153
00:23:41,970 --> 00:23:49,970
And we're going to have all these multiple reflections that are going to be showing up in the air on the left hand side.
于是我们会有所有这些多次反射，出现在左边的空气中。

154
00:23:49,970 --> 00:24:09,970
So what you can see here in this case, due to these multiple reflections, the amount of light that's going to get cumulatively reflected is going to be much, it's going to be more, it's going to be larger than the amount of light or irradiance
所以你在这里可以看到，在这种情况下，由于这些多次反射，累计反射的光量会大得多，会更多，会大于

155
00:24:09,970 --> 00:24:24,970
in the case of the single reflection as we had in the previous case. So the formula that we established on the previous slide, where the reflectance has been defined as a function of the indices of refraction and one and then two,
上一种情况中单次反射的光量或辐照度。所以我们在上一张幻灯片中建立的公式，其中反射率被定义为折射率 n1 和 n2 的函数，

156
00:24:24,970 --> 00:24:37,970
that formula has to be scratched in our case, and we have to establish a different type of a formula that's going to take into account all these multiple infractions that are showing up in the case of an optical window with the two boundaries,
这个公式在我们这里就不适用了，我们必须建立另一种公式，把具有两个边界的光学窗口中出现的所有这些多次反射都考虑进去，

157
00:24:37,970 --> 00:24:48,970
one on the left side and one on the right side. So after a certain derivations, we can come up with a new set of formulas that are shown here on this slide.
左边一个边界，右边一个边界。所以经过一些推导，我们可以得到这张幻灯片上所示的一组新公式。

158
00:24:48,970 --> 00:24:59,970
So the first thing that you're going to calculate is the quantity n sub r that's going to be equal to the ratio of the index of refraction of the window and the medium.
所以你首先要计算的是 n 下标 r 这个量，它等于窗口折射率与介质折射率之比。

159
00:24:59,970 --> 00:25:12,970
So in our case, we have index of refraction of the window, which is going to be equal to 1.6, and then index of refraction of the medium is the index of refraction of the medium that surrounds this window in our case is going to be air.
所以在我们这里，窗口的折射率等于 1.6，而介质的折射率就是这块窗口周围介质的折射率，在我们这里就是空气。

160
00:25:12,970 --> 00:25:33,970
So you're going to take again 1.6 over 1, come up with a value for the n subscript r, and then you're going to substitute the value of this n subscript r factor into the formula on the left hand side and calculate the total reflectance.
所以你还是取 1.6 除以 1，得到 n 下标 r 的值，然后把这个 n 下标 r 因子的值代入左边的公式，计算总反射率。

161
00:25:33,970 --> 00:25:46,970
If you do that, you're going to see that this total reflectance is going to be more than 4% as in the case of a single boundary where the window is of infinite thickness.
如果你这样做，你会看到这个总反射率会大于 4%，后者是窗口无限厚、只有单个边界时的情况。

162
00:25:46,970 --> 00:26:09,970
So the difference, again, between the two formulas, two equations or two cases, is the fact that in the case of the window of finite thickness, we have multiple reflections that have to be taken into account in the total cumulative reflectance that we want to determine in this specific example.
所以这两个公式、两个方程或者说两种情况之间的区别，同样在于，对于有限厚度的窗口，我们有多次反射，必须把它们计入这个具体例子中我们想确定的总累计反射率。

